<title>GERMANY: German building union to set out 1997 wage claim.</title>
<headline>German building union to set out 1997 wage claim.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German's IG-BAU trade union on Tuesday was preparing to unveil its 1997 wage demand for the one million-plus workers in the construction sector, union officials said.</p>
<p>Last April, the union agreed a 1.85 percent pay rise in a deal hailed by economists as pragmatic and positive for the sector.</p>
<p>Employment in the industry has however continued to fall with low economic growth rates and has most recently been hit hard by the severe winter.</p>
<p>IG-BAU officials said the union's main wage committee would be meeting at its headquarters in Frankfurt on Tuesday, after which it would announce its 1997 wage demand at a news conference due from 1230 GMT onwards.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
